Z||000003||82-T/A||12-08-2000||10:18 AM||||Well, he obviously photoshopped it, but I've heard of people doing that all the time.<P>What you do is basically get your car to run really rich.<P>Then you install a rapid fire spark plug somewhere before the beginning of the exhaust tip. You tap it in there somewhere.. and you have a switch connected to it.<P>It ignites the unburned fuel just as it's leaving the exhaust and comes out in flames.<P>I THINK you can also run a fuel line into the back there.. but... I dunno, I would never attempt anything like that on my precious cars.. heh. Besides, I think running rich can burn a piston or whatever else.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
Z||000004||86SE||12-08-2000||12:09 PM||||Yes this is just a photoshop image.  But this car really does shoot flames!  Bluish/orange about 18 inches long.  I took out the cat and now just have to rev it to about 5 grand and let off the gas<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000005||82-T/A||12-08-2000||01:02 PM||||Not to Flame (hah) but just incase you were unaware, thats a really good way to destroy your motor.<P>You could burn a valve or a piston, or any number of other things.<P>It's also REALLY bad to rev your engine that high when it's not in gear IE: there is no load on the motor.<P>A motor should not be revved any more than maybe 3,000 at the most in neutral.<P>Todd||||reg||1
Z||000006||pHoOl||12-08-2000||01:38 PM||||Anybody know of a way to run a fuel line to the pipe?  I thought of doing it that way whether i had a seperate little fuel system for the flames or not i haven't thought of yet.  But my concern would be the flame "backdrafting" (not sure if that's the right term) but you get the idea.  you shoot flames out the back, but it travels to the gas tank or whatever the fuel is in.  BOOOOOM<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||12-08-2000||01:57 PM||||the 4cyl (87 Fiero) a friend of mine runs at the local 1/4 (Commerece International Raceway) sure his car is slow but the best launches have been at 4500+ they don't have any torque and need the flywheel speed/rotational mass to launch him off the line. (and imports tach to well over 6000 at the tree/street light on a launch)  you'd be hard pressed to burn the valves in a 2.8 with an exhaust system on it... and looking at 86SEs car.. it looks like a stock muffler.. it's a backpressure monster! 2.5" systems i've run are great..(headers and all) never had any fuel realated issues, no valvetrain problems and neither cars have cats. and one had nitrous. the other will soon.. <P><BR>86.. add a pair of spark plugs to the tail pipes and then take us some pics.. or just running NOS without a cat ..      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> you'll have a nice flame then! SWEET!   fun with Photoshop!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  i love that yellow!! <P><BR>you don't have to have MORE fuel in the exhaust system just spark.. ditch the cat and tap in a pair of spark plugs and switched power, coil.. the unspent fuel the motor spits out will be ignited by the additional plugs and then you'll have the flames your looking for...  look here for the pics... <BR> <A HREF="http://www.picturetrail.com/gallery/view?p=999&gid=118206&uid=19674" TARGET=_blank>http://www.picturetrail.com/gallery/view?p=999&gid=118206&uid=19674</A> <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-08-2000).]||||reg||1
