Z||000010||Eric_PA||12-09-2000||10:37 AM||||This post reminded me of a time I was out in Pottstown where everyone goes to cruise there cars. There was this guy with a VW Golf with a VR6 installed into it. He hooked up a copper line to his exhaust and pumped antifreeze to it. Yes I said antifreeze. He would rev the engine up, hit the switch and would have an instant cloud of white smoke. I was behind him when he did it. I couldn't see anything. I had to stop and ask him why the #$%@ he did this. He told me that this way people think he has a blown engine and can whoop them. I was like ok then. But he showed me haw he did it. he ran a line from his windsheild wiper washer fluid container and made a fitting on the header. I thought to myself poor catalitic converter and why would someone do this.||||reg||10
